  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the woman with blood on her lip as the embodiment of the misogynistic trope",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the woman with blood on her lip, interpreting her as the literalized subject of the meme's darkly humorous analogy. The user sees themselves as the person who might be expected to 'fix' problems through violence, or as the victim of such expectations, by identifying with the woman's injury and distress. The projection is implicit, not explicit (no deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you'), but the user's identification with the woman's role in the meme's narrative is the core of the semiotic projection. The user is projected onto the 'woman' entity, which is the central visual material and the subject of the misogynistic stereotype being depicted.",
